.TH LIBMPQ__FILE_VERIFY 3 2026-09-10 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__file_verify \- explicitly compare stored file checksums
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__file_verify("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive",
.BI "        uint32_t       " "file_number",
.BI "        uint32_t       " "verify_flags",
.BI "        uint32_t      *" "mismatches"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Explicitly verify requested file CRC32, file MD5, and sector Adler-32
checksums for an archive member. Complete file reads automatically check usable
sector Adler-32 values, and complete lossless reads automatically check
available CRC32/MD5 metadata. This interface lets callers select checks and
returns mismatches as bits. Verification is independent of writer policy.
.SS "Requested Checks"
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_FILE_CRC32 requests CRC32 and LIBMPQ_VERIFY_FILE_MD5 requests
MD5. LIBMPQ_VERIFY_SECTOR_CRC requests sector checksums, and
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_ALL requests all three. These bits also identify mismatches;
they are not LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_* presence flags. Unknown request bits are
rejected. A zero request is a no-op after validating the reader and file number.
.SS "File CRC32 and MD5"
Available values from (attributes) are compared against the complete logical
uncompressed file contents, not compressed or encrypted storage.
Lossless files match the writer's source-byte checksums. Lossy ADPCM can
produce different bytes and therefore legitimately report mismatches.
Empty files use the standard empty CRC32 and MD5 values.
.PP
The implementation reads one logical block at a time; a single-unit file
requires its full unpacked block buffer. FILETIME and PATCH_BIT are not verified.
.SS "Sector Adler-32"
MPQ sector CRCs are Adler-32 checksums over stored sectors after decryption
and before decompression. Their table may be compressed but is not encrypted.
Absent tables and zero or all-ones checksum entries are skipped. Single-unit
files have no sector checksum table. Complete file reads automatically compare
usable sector entries, including before lossy ADPCM decoding; malformed optional
tables are skipped during normal extraction. This explicit interface continues
to report sector metadata errors and per-check mismatches.
.SS "Missing Metadata"
Missing (attributes) is an error when either file checksum is requested.
Sector-only requests do not require (attributes). Requested file checksums
absent from the selected row are skipped, including omitted legacy rows.
Zero mismatch bits mean no mismatch was detected, not that checksums existed.
Use \fBlibmpq__file_attributes\fP() to inspect per-file availability when
required. Checksums are not cryptographic authentication.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns LIBMPQ_SUCCESS when the operation completes, even on mismatch.
The output in *mismatches is a subset of verify_flags, using the same
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_SECTOR_CRC, LIBMPQ_VERIFY_FILE_CRC32, and LIBMPQ_VERIFY_FILE_MD5
bits. A set bit means a requested, available checksum mismatched.
A clear bit means the checksum matched or was unavailable/skipped.
.PP
Operation failures return a negative libmpq error and leave *mismatches zero,
even if earlier sectors had mismatches. Bits are published only after the
complete operation succeeds.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST means a NULL argument, invalid file number, or absent
attributes. LIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED means a writer handle was supplied.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT means unknown request bits or malformed metadata.
Read, seek, decoding, size, and allocation failures are reported as errors.
When mismatches is non-NULL it is initialized before validation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__block_verify (3),
.BR libmpq__file_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__file_read (3)
